Recently, I suggested that characters who find wizard bones levels (i.e. bones
levels created in debugging mode) would not get scored. When I said that there
should be an option for setting wizard bones levels on/off, of course I meant
that this option should be _user_definable, not a compile-time option!

You could set it at the beginning of a game like pet type or whatever. The 
default would be !wiz_bones
And characters who find those levels (have set the option to wiz_bones) would
leave behind bones files which would be considered wizard bones levels by
this option etc.

Another way to prevent this kind of cheating would be to tag every item on
a wizard bones level WIZ_ITEM and when a player (in a scoring mode) tries
to pick up a WIZ_ITEM, he will get:
	
"Warning! A Wizard mode item! If you pick it up, your game will not be scored!
 Pick it up anyway? (y/n) n"

Pets or monsters wouldn't touch WIZ_ITEMs either. The tag will remain in the
item forever after it has been put there, so if someone picks up a WIZ_ITEM
and then dies, another character cannot cheat using their bones files...

How's about hat?

